<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Balhaego</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1784">1784</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Balhaego, &quot;A Study of Balhae&quot;, is a history of the kingdom of Balhae written by the Joseon scholar <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yu-deuk-gong">Yu Deuk-gong</a> and completed in 1784. Drawing on Chinese, Korean and Japanese sources, it treated Balhae as a Korean state and coined the idea of a period of Northern and Southern States with Unified Silla, which shaped later Korean historiography.</p></div>
